# Generated parquet datasets — not checked in.
# Anchored to this dir (leading /) so they ONLY match the data dirs at
# testdata/<dataset>.sf<N>/ and NOT the committed goldens under
# testdata/goldens/<dataset>.sf<N>/ (the unanchored form caught those too).
/tpch.sf*/
/tpcds.sf*/

# Calibration output: the text is committed, the captures are not, and the line between
# them is size against regenerability. The three .tsv files and the panels are the
# measurement, rewritten in place by each collection so `git diff` shows how the numbers
# moved; llm-wiki names the script that writes each. Ignored: the nsys exports, hundreds
# of megabytes of binary git cannot diff, and the counters pass's own record, whose
# microseconds are a profiler's.
# Deny-by-default, so a new file here is ignored until someone says otherwise. The
# directory and its contents are re-included as two lines: git re-includes a directory
# happily, but its own documented rule says a file under an excluded parent cannot be, and
# third-party matchers implement that rule and grey out plots/ entirely.
/calibration/*
!/calibration/records.tsv
!/calibration/hbm.tsv
!/calibration/calls.tsv
!/calibration/plots/
!/calibration/plots/**
